cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Jitterbug in your research, please cite the PAM 2022 paper below."
type: software
title: "Jitterbug: Framework for Jitter-Based Congestion Inference"
abstract: "Jitterbug infers network congestion from Round-Trip Time (RTT) time series. It computes minimum-RTT intervals, detects change points, and classifies each period as congested or not using a latency jump and either jitter dispersion or a Kolmogorov-Smirnov test."
